      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The regulator cares less about the *technical state* of the data in the background and more about the *effectiveness of your commitment* to erasure. If you have a documented, auditable process—like tagging it as \"Do Not Use\"—that proves you are actively managing the residual data, you are generally in a much safer position. You must be able to demonstrate to the regulator that the data is effectively inaccessible and will be purged according to your defined timeline. Failing to have a clear, documented plan for those \"pockets\" is where the real risk lies.",
